@*
    Renders markdown text as formatted HTML (headings, bold, lists, tables, code blocks).

    Used for AI assistant answers, which arrive as markdown. The conversion — including
    the XSS sanitisation — lives in MarkdownRenderer so it can be unit tested on its own;
    this component only wraps the result in a styled container.

    The .markdown-body class (app.css) tames the spacing of the generated HTML so that
    headings and lists do not blow up the size of a chat bubble.
*@

<div class="markdown-body @Class">@((MarkupString)MarkdownRenderer.ToSafeHtml(Content))</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>
    /// Raw markdown to render. Null or whitespace renders an empty container.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? Content { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// Extra CSS classes appended to the container (spacing utilities, etc.).
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? Class { get; set; }
}
